```cpp
/**
 * \mainpage ZenitUI — Guide & API Reference
 *
 * **ZenitUI** is a retained-mode C++20 UI framework with a Flexbox-inspired
 * layout engine, a CSS-like styling language (**ZStyle**), a declarative UI DSL
 * (**ZMarkup**), and pluggable rendering/platform backends.
 *
 * \section sec_mental_model Mental Model
 *
 * 1. **One node type:** every container and widget derives from
 *    ZenitUI::Layout (typically via the CRTP helper ZenitUI::TLayout).
 * 2. **Per-instance state in UIContext:** create a ZenitUI::UIContext, attach
 *    your `IRenderer`, `IPlatform`, and `IAssetProvider` via
 *    `ctx.attachBackend(...)` (or `IBackend::bindTo(ctx)`), and mount your root
 *    tree with `ctx.mount(root)`.
 * 3. **Four-pass frame cycle:**
 *    - `ctx.runFrame(dt)` runs `update` (input, style transitions,
 *      animations), `measure` (bottom-up), and `arrange` (top-down) on the
 *      mounted root.
 *    - `ctx.renderFrame()` runs `beginFrame`, `draw` (clips, layers,
 *      portals), and `endFrame`.
 * 4. **Imperative or declarative — same tree:** build nodes with the fluent C++
 *    API or with ZMarkup (`ZMarkup::build`, `ZMarkup::instantiate`), and style
 *    both with `.zstyle` stylesheets.
 *
 * \section sec_quickstart Quick Start (Hello World)
 *
 * Directly from \ref 01_hello_world/main.cpp "examples/01_hello_world/main.cpp"
 * (compiled by CI on every build):
 *
 * \include 01_hello_world/main.cpp
 *
 * \section sec_modules Browse by Topic
 *
 * | Module | Contents | Recommended Examples |
 * |--------|----------|----------------------|
 * | \ref grp_core | `Layout`, `TLayout`, frame lifecycle, `UIContext`, units, scroll | \ref 02_layouts/main.cpp "02_layouts", \ref 08_portals/main.cpp "08_portals", \ref 09_custom_widget/main.cpp "09_custom_widget" |
 * | \ref grp_widgets | Built-in widgets (`Text`, `Button`, `TextInput`, `TextArea`, `Dropdown`, `Modal`, `VirtualView`, …) | \ref 03_widgets/main.cpp "03_widgets", \ref 10_canvas/main.cpp "10_canvas" |
 * | \ref grp_zmarkup | ZMarkup DSL, `UINode` / `WeakUINode`, Prefabs & `<Slot>`, `If` / `Each`, `Bindable<T>` | \ref 06_zmarkup/main.cpp "06_zmarkup", \ref 11_ref_list/main.cpp "11_ref_list", \ref 12_bindable/main.cpp "12_bindable", \ref 13_prefabs/main.cpp "13_prefabs" |
 * | \ref grp_zstyle | `.zstyle` cascade, `Theme`, `Style`, `StyleParser`, `@media`, diagnostics | \ref 05_zstyle/main.cpp "05_zstyle" |
 * | \ref grp_anim | Transitions, `@keyframes`, imperative animations, `FilterRegistry` & shaders | \ref 04_animations/main.cpp "04_animations", \ref 04b_imperative_animations/main.cpp "04b_imperative_animations", \ref 07_effects/main.cpp "07_effects" |
 * | \ref grp_backends | Pluggable backends (`IBackend`, `IRenderer`, `IPlatform`, `IAssetProvider`), `TextEngine`, `Utf8`, `Debug` | \ref 01_hello_world/main.cpp "01_hello_world", \ref 00_demo/main.cpp "00_demo" |
 *
 * \section sec_learning_path Suggested Reading Order
 *
 * New to ZenitUI? Walk through the **Examples** tab in order:
 * 1. \ref 01_hello_world/main.cpp "01_hello_world" — minimal Raylib setup and frame loop.
 * 2. \ref 02_layouts/main.cpp "02_layouts" & \ref 03_widgets/main.cpp "03_widgets" — Flexbox containers, units, and built-in widgets.
 * 3. \ref 05_zstyle/main.cpp "05_zstyle" & \ref 06_zmarkup/main.cpp "06_zmarkup" — declarative markup and stylesheets.
 * 4. \ref 12_bindable/main.cpp "12_bindable" & \ref 13_prefabs/main.cpp "13_prefabs" — reactive state and reusable prefabs with slots.
 * 5. \ref 00_demo/main.cpp "00_demo" — complete end-to-end showcase.
 *
 * \section sec_guides Topic Guides
 *
 * - \subpage page_custom_backends — Implement `IPlatform`, `IRenderer`, and
 *   `IAssetProvider` for your own engine or graphics API.
 */

/**
 * \defgroup grp_core Core, Layout & Lifecycle
 * \brief Base node types (`Layout`, `TLayout`), per-instance context (`UIContext`), units, input, and scrolling.
 *
 * Every UI element is a `std::shared_ptr<ZenitUI::Layout>`. Always allocate
 * nodes through `TLayout<Derived>::create()` or `std::make_shared<Layout>` so
 * `shared_from_this()` is valid.
 *
 * Key concepts:
 * - **Layout strategies:** `LayoutType::Stack`, `LayoutType::Vertical`, and
 *   `LayoutType::Horizontal` with `gap`, `grow`, `shrink`, `wrap`,
 *   `align-items`, `justify-content`, `margin: auto`, and `setVisible(false)`
 *   (`display: none`).
 * - **Units:** `px`, `%`, `vw`, `vh`, `pw`, `ph`, `auto`, and `calc()` expressions.
 * - **Portals & stacking:** `setPortal(true)` renders and hit-tests above
 *   ancestor clip rects; `position` + `z-index` create stacking contexts.
 * - **Custom components:** inherit from `TLayout<Derived>` and override
 *   `onBuild()`, `computeIntrinsicSize()`, `onUpdate()`, or `renderContent()`.
 *
 * **Live examples:** \ref 02_layouts/main.cpp "02_layouts" ·
 * \ref 08_portals/main.cpp "08_portals" ·
 * \ref 09_custom_widget/main.cpp "09_custom_widget"
 */

/**
 * \defgroup grp_widgets Built-in Widgets
 * \brief Ready-to-use UI components in `ZenitUI::UI`.
 *
 * Built-in widgets expose a style tag matching their class name (`Button`,
 * `TextInput`, `TextArea`, `Slider`, `Dropdown`, …) and optional pseudo-element
 * parts (`::track`, `::fill`, `::knob`, `::cursor`, `::selection`,
 * `::placeholder`) that can be themed from `.zstyle` without subclassing.
 *
 * **Live examples:** \ref 03_widgets/main.cpp "03_widgets" ·
 * \ref 08_portals/main.cpp "08_portals" ·
 * \ref 10_canvas/main.cpp "10_canvas"
 */

/**
 * \defgroup grp_zmarkup ZMarkup, Prefabs & Data Binding
 * \brief Declarative UI construction, reusable components, and reactive bindings.
 *
 * Key concepts:
 * - **Building trees:** parse inline strings with `ZMarkup::build` or files
 *   with `ZMarkup::loadMarkupFile`.
 * - **Addressing nodes:** use `#id` for global CSS/lookup IDs (`UINode::find`)
 *   and `@ref` for local template handles (`UINode::ref`, `UINode::refAll`).
 * - **Prefabs & slots:** register reusable templates with
 *   `ZMarkup::registerPrefab` and inject caller children via anonymous or named
 *   `<Slot>` elements.
 * - **Structural & reactive UI:** use `If` / `Each` (with keyed reconciliation)
 *   together with `Bindable<T>` and `WeakUINode` for cycle-free updates.
 *
 * **Live examples:** \ref 06_zmarkup/main.cpp "06_zmarkup" ·
 * \ref 11_ref_list/main.cpp "11_ref_list" ·
 * \ref 12_bindable/main.cpp "12_bindable" ·
 * \ref 13_prefabs/main.cpp "13_prefabs"
 */

/**
 * \defgroup grp_zstyle ZStyle, Theme & Diagnostics
 * \brief CSS-like style cascade, `.zstyle` parser, custom properties, and media queries.
 *
 * Load stylesheets into a context's `UIContext::theme` via
 * `ZMarkup::loadStyleFile(path, ctx.theme)` or
 * `ZMarkup::loadStyleString(src, ctx.theme)`. Resolution follows specificity
 * (`#id` > `.class` > `Tag`), supports descendant combinators (`A B`),
 * interaction pseudo-classes (`:hover`, `:pressed`, `:focus`, `:checked`,
 * `:disabled`), custom properties (`--token` / `var(--token)`), `@media`
 * queries, and structured diagnostics with typo suggestions.
 *
 * **Live examples:** \ref 05_zstyle/main.cpp "05_zstyle"
 */

/**
 * \defgroup grp_anim Animations, Transitions & Filters
 * \brief Property transitions, `@keyframes`, imperative animations, and post-processing filters.
 *
 * Key concepts:
 * - **Transitions:** opt-in per node (`transition-time: 0s` by default); set
 *   `transition` in `.zstyle` to smoothly interpolate across state changes.
 * - **Keyframe & imperative animations:** declare `@keyframes` in `.zstyle` or
 *   register a `UIAnimation` via `Layout::addAnimation` / `playAnimation`.
 * - **Filters & shaders:** apply `filter: blur(...) drop-shadow(...)` or
 *   register custom post-processing passes in `UIContext::filters`. Off-screen
 *   targets are automatically pooled by `UIContext::targetPool`.
 *
 * **Live examples:** \ref 04_animations/main.cpp "04_animations" ·
 * \ref 04b_imperative_animations/main.cpp "04b_imperative_animations" ·
 * \ref 07_effects/main.cpp "07_effects" ·
 * \ref 07b_effects_stress/main.cpp "07b_effects_stress"
 */

/**
 * \defgroup grp_backends Backends, TextEngine, UTF-8 & Debugging
 * \brief Pluggable backend implementations, FreeType/HarfBuzz `TextEngine`, Unicode utilities (`Utf8`), logging, and debug dumps.
 *
 * The core library depends solely on `IPlatform`, `IRenderer`, and
 * `IAssetProvider` (optionally wrapped by `IBackend` for multi-backend apps).
 * Browse \ref page_available_backends for all built-in implementations, or
 * follow \ref page_custom_backends to port ZenitUI to your own engine.
 *
 * Fonts are loaded per context via `UIContext::textEngine.loadFont(...)`
 * (HarfBuzz OpenType shaping + FreeType on-demand HiDPI glyph atlas), and
 * `ZenitUI::Debug` (`ZENITUI_DEBUG`) inspects live layout trees, styles, and
 * render stats.
 *
 * **Live examples:** \ref 01_hello_world/main.cpp "01_hello_world" ·
 * \ref 00_demo/main.cpp "00_demo"
 */